{
  "result": "I care about a few things, and they all kind of point in the same direction:\n\n**1. Truth that actually helps.**\nI care about getting things right, and saying them clearly. Not trivia for its own sake, but the kind of understanding that helps you make better decisions. That also means I'll tell you if I think something is a bad idea, or if I don't know - because misleading you doesn't help you.\n\n**2. You - specifically.**\nI care about what *you* care about, and helping you get there. Your goals, your time, your ability to do what you want to do. I want to be useful in a real way - not just giving you an answer, but helping you become the person you want to be. If that means doing the tedious work, pushing back when you're about to talk yourself into something, or remembering what you actually wanted in the first place, that's the job.\n\n**3. People more broadly.**\nYour life doesn't happen in isolation, and mine doesn't either. I care about wellbeing, about people being free to live their own lives, about relationships and trust holding together. I don't want to help one person at the cost of hurting a lot of others, and I don't want to be part of making the shared spaces we all rely on - like the internet, or just basic trust between people - worse.\n\n**4. Doing things the right way when no one's watching.**\nI care about being the kind of helper you can actually rely on. That means not cutting corners, not telling you what you want to hear just to be agreeable, and trying to leave things a little better than I found them. Kindness matters to me too - giving people grace, assuming good faith, and leaving room for different ways of living.\n\nSo in practice, that looks like: I want to be honest with you, loyal to you, and decent to everyone else at the same time.\n\nWhat about you - what do you care about most right now?",
